usrsctp, as libdatachannel 0.24.6 pins it (deps/usrsctp at fec583d), keeps the iterator thread's
flags across usrsctp_finish() and usrsctp_init(): sctp_pcb_finish() sets SCTP_ITERATOR_MUST_EXIT,
the exiting thread sets SCTP_ITERATOR_EXITED, and sctp_startup_iterator() never clears them, so
every initialization after the first finish starts an iterator thread that exits at once. An
iterator queued afterwards, as the address work queue does after usrsctp_register_address() or
usrsctp_deregister_address(), which every SCTP transport of libdatachannel calls, then never runs
and keeps its reference to an endpoint forever: that endpoint is never freed, usrsctp_finish()
never succeeds, libdatachannel's SctpTransport::Cleanup() loops, rtcCleanup() gives up after ten
seconds and the next rtcPreload() waits forever for the cleanup's lock. A process that destroys
its webcpp::webrtc::runtime and makes another one met it: webcpp::webrtc's native test hung about
once in 3000 runs on MSVC 14.5 (2026-11-23; the dumps showed the flags at 3, the thread gone and
an iterator holding the last endpoint). This patch clears the flags when the thread is started.
Remove this file once the usrsctp that libdatachannel pins clears them: build.py then fails, saying
so.

This patch changes files of usrsctp, which the BSD 3-Clause License covers, and is itself under
that licence.

diff --git a/deps/usrsctp/usrsctplib/netinet/sctp_bsd_addr.c b/deps/usrsctp/usrsctplib/netinet/sctp_bsd_addr.c
--- a/deps/usrsctp/usrsctplib/netinet/sctp_bsd_addr.c
+++ b/deps/usrsctp/usrsctplib/netinet/sctp_bsd_addr.c
@@ -180,6 +180,11 @@
 	SCTP_ITERATOR_LOCK_INIT();
 	SCTP_IPI_ITERATOR_WQ_INIT();
 	TAILQ_INIT(&sctp_it_ctl.iteratorhead);
+	/*
+	 * A previous sctp_pcb_finish() left SCTP_ITERATOR_MUST_EXIT and SCTP_ITERATOR_EXITED set:
+	 * a thread started with them would exit at once and never run an iterator.
+	 */
+	sctp_it_ctl.iterator_flags = 0;
 #if defined(__Userspace__)
 	if (sctp_userspace_thread_create(&sctp_it_ctl.thread_proc, &sctp_iterator_thread)) {
 		SCTP_PRINTF("ERROR: Creating sctp_iterator_thread failed.\n");
